# Shell scripts and the Makefile MUST be LF.
#  - A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally
#    named '/bin/bash<CR>', and the postgres entrypoint then fails at
#    first boot with 'cannot execute: required file not found'.
#  - A trailing CR on a Makefile recipe line becomes part of the command
#    make hands to the shell.
# Both cost an hour the first time. Pinned here so they cannot recur.
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
